     written — the deploy path and every mid-run ground change — and `Screens`
     has never had a `loading` method, so the optional-call operator swallowed
     both. What a player saw while a terrain heightfield, a Rapier world, every
     instanced field and up to 224 props were built was the menu going away and
     nothing arriving: 350 ms warm, 3.8 s cold, on a blank page.

     It carries the SAME plate the menu does, which is the player's instruction
     — "it will be the background for any non-in game menu or screen" — and it
     costs nothing extra to do so: `.menu-bg`'s file is already fetched and
     decoded by the time anybody can press Deploy, so this is a second element
     naming a warm cache entry rather than a second download. The boot screen is
     the one screen that may NOT do this, and index.html says why above it.

     The wordmark rides above the bar because this screen is on for seconds and
     is the last thing between the menu and the game — it is a title card, not a
