  <!--
    THE GUARD ROSE. Four petals round the reticle, one lit.

    A discrete state the player cannot see is a state they cannot play, and
    directional blocking is nothing but a discrete state — so this is not
    decoration, it is the readout for the whole mechanic. It sits ON the reticle
    rather than in a corner because that is where the eye already is while you
    are being shot at, and it is empty (all four dim) whenever no guard is up,
    so "I have no guard" reads as a state rather than as an absence.

    The styles are inline rather than in styles.css because this element is
    owned by the same change as the mechanic, and because a HUD readout that
    is half in one file and half in another is how one of them goes stale.
  -->
  <style>
    #guard-rose { position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 50%; width: 168px; height: 168px;
      transform: translate(-50%, -50%); pointer-events: none; opacity: 0;
      transition: opacity .16s ease; }
    #guard-rose.on { opacity: 1; }
    #guard-rose .pet { fill: rgba(190, 225, 255, .085); stroke: rgba(190, 225, 255, .18);
      stroke-width: .8; transition: fill .09s linear, stroke .09s linear; }
    /* The lit petal is the guard you are holding. */
    #guard-rose .pet.sel { fill: rgba(150, 225, 255, .40); stroke: rgba(200, 245, 255, .95); }
    /* …and while the parry window is open it is hotter, because the difference
       between a block and a riposte is 200 ms and nothing else. */
    #guard-rose.parry .pet.sel { fill: rgba(255, 232, 150, .62); stroke: rgba(255, 246, 205, 1); }
    /* The petal the NEXT bolt wants — a dashed outline, never a fill, so it
       cannot be mistaken for the guard you are actually holding. This is how
       the mapping from "where it came from" to "which way to flick" gets
       learned by looking instead of by dying. */
    #guard-rose .pet.want { stroke: rgba(255, 140, 120, .95); stroke-width: 1.6;
      stroke-dasharray: 3 2.5; }
  </style>
  <svg id="guard-rose" viewBox="-50 -50 100 100" aria-hidden="true">
    <path class="pet" data-zone="high"  d="M-13 -18 L0 -40 L13 -18 A22 22 0 0 0 -13 -18 Z"></path>
    <path class="pet" data-zone="low"   d="M-13 18 L0 40 L13 18 A22 22 0 0 1 -13 18 Z"></path>
    <path class="pet" data-zone="left"  d="M-18 -13 L-40 0 L-18 13 A22 22 0 0 1 -18 -13 Z"></path>
