<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     THE MEDITATION — the Holocron.

     IT WAS A CONSTELLATION, and it was renamed because the player asked what
     stars had to do with any of it: "you're becoming more and more attuned to
     the force or good/evil side — wtf does that have to do with stars and
     constellations". That is a fair question and the honest answer is that the
     picture came first (a node graph reads as a star chart) and the fiction was
     bent to fit it. A holocron is the same picture with the right fiction under
     it — a crystal lattice you attune to and that teaches you — so the drawing
     did not change and every word around it did. The lattice is grouped into
     six CURRENTS of the Force, each a teaching; a node is a FACET, and you WAKE
     one rather than lighting it. The currency is still Insight, which was
     always right.

     Raised mid-run by kneeling (hold Crouch, still, with nothing near you) and
     between runs from the Temple. The world behind it is STOPPED and still
     drawn, and there is no blur over it: the whole reason this is reached by
     kneeling rather than by a menu key is that it happens in the place you were
     standing, and your own Jedi is knelt in the middle of it.
     src/ui/SkillTree.js draws it; src/game/LivingForce.js decides everything
     it is allowed to say.
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div id="meditation" class="screen hidden">
  <div class="med-wrap">
    <header class="med-head">
      <div>
        <h2 id="med-title">Connect to the Force</h2>
        <p class="hint" id="med-sub"></p>
      </div>
